& [ReusablePathMechanics]
  + workspace admission requires absolute already-canonical nonsymlink directories and rejects equality ancestor and descendant overlap between principal and candidate workspaces
  + it binds principal candidate repository common and candidate Git directory paths into a content-addressed admission receipt
  + allowed relative paths reject dot dot-dot colon NUL backslash and .git segments and require sorted unique nonoverlapping values
  + topology forms provide strict root and descendant metadata claim grammar while later supplied-carrier modules can bind stronger observed identities under their own authority
  + live_codex validates absolute canonical working directories but does not model distinct state canary temporary evidence or recovery roots

& [Insufficiencies]
  + final-component nonsymlink and canonical-path checks alone do not prove every ancestor is free of reparse substitution or bind a stable volume and file identity
  + lexical starts_with overlap is not by itself a Windows case-normalized physical identity proof
  + candidate workspace admission binds Git worktree roles and cannot silently add App Server state canary executable-package or evidence-root roles
  + topology metadata claims are not physical observations and current supplied carrier types remain separately acquired inputs
  + existing live_codex uses ambient state locations and provides no cleanup or recovery owner

& [B1RootRoleGrammar]
  + bind exact canonical principal workspace candidate workspace repository common directory candidate Git directory App Server state root SQLite state root canary root prospective evidence root executable package root and schema-output root roles
  + every role carries canonical path text role kind required pre-state digest and separately supplied strongest available topology identity without claiming physical truth from metadata alone
  + require exact equality containment or separation for every ordered role pair rather than applying one blanket nonoverlap rule
  + state SQLite canary and schema-output roots may be declared descendants of one externally prepared disposable container while principal Git executable-package and evidence roots remain separated according to their exact roles
  + deny any equality or containment involving the principal workspace Git common directory Git directory executable package root user CODEX_HOME or ambient temporary directory unless the closed relation matrix explicitly requires it
  + refuse root substitution identity drift unexpected pre-state membership symlink reparse ambiguity case-fold collision path-length overflow or role duplication before process launch

& [PreparationAndRecoveryAuthority]
  + a read-only B1 preflight cannot create populate clean delete or recover its own disposable roots without contradicting its no-mutation authority
  + one separate fixture-preparation commission must create the exact empty or canary-populated roots and issue their pre-state identities before B1
  + one named recovery owner outside the B1 process receives the fixture commission cleanup conditions root identities and operator-visible refusal state
  + B1 may observe and report post-state only under its signed observation commission and must never run cleanup on success timeout refusal or interruption
  + cleanup is a later separately authorized action only after evidence is durably captured and every descendant is proven terminal
  + inability to prove terminal descendants or exact root identity leaves the fixture quarantined for the recovery owner rather than guessed deletion

& [Delineation]
  + disposable describes lifecycle ownership and eventual cleanup eligibility not permission for B1 to mutate or delete
  + an evidence root is prospective until a separately authorized evidence producer writes after B1; B1 itself returns an in-memory bounded observation
  + exact paths cannot be chosen from ambient TEMP CODEX_HOME current directory recency or convenience
  + current validators are predecessor design evidence and cannot be widened under B1 without a signed exact type and support matrix

& [GapDelta]
  + G06 changes from unspecified disposable roots and recovery owner to a closed role set relation-matrix requirement separate preparation commission named recovery owner quarantine rule and cleanup nonauthority
  + G06 remains unresolved for exact current paths strong identities pre-state fixture contents relation values preparation commission recovery-owner identity cleanup commission and live post-state receipts
  + G03 G04 G05 remain narrowed_not_closed while G01 G02 and G07 remain open

& [StopRules]
  + do not create canonicalize enumerate hash modify remove or clean any live directory or environment state under this source
  + do not use the repository root user profile home ambient temporary root executable package or Git directory as an inferred disposable root
  + do not let B1 own preparation evidence writing cleanup recovery quarantine release or deletion capability

& [Next]
  + hash and manifest this root inventory
  + preserve G06 as narrowed_not_closed
  + require operator-supplied exact prepared-root and recovery-owner source together with executable selection before final B1 SJS
